import XCTest
@testable import HRVCore

/// The phase clock, against the reference engine.
///
/// **This file is generated** by `tools/export-swift-fixtures.mjs` in the
/// breathing-poc repo.
///
/// The exercises are chosen for the shapes that behave differently rather than
/// to sample the catalogue: no holds, one hold, two holds, a two-cycle
/// alternating practice, and one whose phases are under a second — the case that
/// broke the region windows once and is the reason they are capped.
///
/// The instants include every phase boundary exactly, and a nanosecond either
/// side of each. That is where the rule "the last phase owns its closing
/// instant" lives, and it is reachable only through floating point, so a port
/// can get it wrong and be correct everywhere a human would look.
